  "preamble": "Change of the voiceless alveolar stop [t] to the voiceless labiodental fricative [f], combining spirantization with a shift to labial place. The documented case is Rotuman, where Proto-Oceanic *t became f (*kutu 'louse' > ʻufu, *qoti 'finished' > ofi). English th-fronting (θ > f) is a different change and is filed under th_vless_to_f.",
